The '''Confederalist Party''' ({{Lang-bl|Partido Confederalista}}) was a [[W:Classical liberalism|classical liberal]] political party in Balisca. 

The party consolidated confederal power through it's dominance in [[Cerdanya]] and [[Hesperia]] in the aftermath of the [[Cantonal Revolution]], where [[Conservatism in Balisca|conservative]] backlash to the [[W:Cantonalism|cantonalist]] reforms had been the strongest. Under the Confederalists, Balisca established itself as a [[W:International neutrality|neutral power]] in international policy, encouraged foreign investment, promoted industrialization and embarked on an massive program to attract immigrants on the heels of the [[Industrial Revolution in Balisca]], resulting in an [[Great Migration (Balisca)|unprecedented wave]] of immigrants to Balisca and significant Old World influence in Baliscan economic and social policy. During the second half of the 19th century the Cerdanyan and Hesperian industry grew exponentially and by 1900, Balisca was an industrial world leader along with Britain, [[Germany]] and the [[United States]].

It was dissolved in the aftermath of the [[Baliscan Revolution]].

